SUMMARY:Look to Windward - Ian M. Banks
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi all\,\n\nSo glad to have our Iain M. 
 Banks selection finalized for November. As we’ve discussed previously\, 
 the books in the Culture series are connected\, but don’t necessarily ne
 ed to be read in order. The Club really enjoyed Book 2\, *The Player of Ga
 mes*\, and I’m curious to see where in the universe we land with Book 7\
 , 2000’s *Look to Windward*.\n\n[sophyanempire](https://sophyanempire.wo
 rdpress.com/2012/03/08/look-to-windward-iain-m-banks-orbit-2000/) has a so
 lid review of this entry in the Culture series\, calling *Look to Windward
 * “exciting\, tense\, sad and heroic.” She notes that from there\, “
 the book grows in scope\, showing multiple perspectives\, almost all of th
 em from a non-human alien point of view.”\n\n[The Guardian](https://www.
 theguardian.com/books/2000/sep/02/sciencefictionfantasyandhorror.iainbanks
 ) also has a great review from when the book was first published. Phil Dao
 ust writes that “Banks has tremendous fun with his giant canvas” in *W
 indward*.\n\nTo join a Book Club meeting\, all you will need is YOURSELF. 
 If you haven’t had a chance to finish the book\, we still would love for
  you to join us in the discussion.\n\nNot able to join us in person for ev
 ents? [The Sci Fi Book Club is on Discord](https://discord.gg/B9NMnC2F). J
 oin us and keep the conversation going.\n\nA reminder that Book Club takes
  a break each October\, so while Look to Windward has a fairly large page 
 count\, we’ll essentially have two months to read our pick.\n\nCheers\,\
 n\nJon
